<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  TEST RIDERS for the WildMesh3D mounts (#794, docs/features/wildmesh-mounts.md), 2026-10-14.

  Clones that ride the five horse-skeleton reskins, so their retargeted clips can be watched in a Custom Battle.
  Spawn one with:
      taom.spawn_troops taom_test_wildmesh_<animal>_rider 5 ally
  where <animal> is boar, warthog, mountaingoat, deer or moose.
  The boar, warthog and goat riders are ironpass_ram_rider (Erebor, race dwarf), with the light ram barding on
  roster 1 and the heavy one on roster 2 (Mike, 2026-10-14: ram harnesses for the dwarf mounts); the deer and
  moose riders are mirkwood_rochenlas with the elk saddle. Every Horse slot has its harness (MOUNT_WITHOUT_HARNESS),
  and the three dwarf mounts are in DWARF_MOUNT_IDS (MOUNTED_DWARF).

  Registered for CustomGame ONLY (Main/_Module/SubModule.xml), so no campaign or save loads them. They are NOT
  hidden from the Custom Battle army picker: it lists them under the Erebor and Mirkwood cavalry, because they
  are Soldiers (ArmyCompositionGroupVM lists every IsSoldier and not IsObsolete character).
  The file sits in test_riders/, not troops/, so tools that glob troops/troops_*.xml do not read it.

  RELEASE: /release step 5 (git grep -l taom_test_, run over Main/_Module) blocks a player release while this
  file exists. Delete this file and its SubModule.xml block before one.
-->

